    passageEn: 'Decarbonizing global civilization represents the paramount existential technological undertaking of our century. While wind and solar generate exponentially expanding shares of zero-carbon power, next-generation deep geothermal and long-duration battery storage shore up grid stability. On the revolutionary frontier of physics, nuclear fusion aims to replicate the stellar power generator fueling our sun. Inside magnetic confinement tokamak chambers, isotopes of deuterium and tritium are heated past one hundred million degrees Celsius into plasma, fusing into helium while releasing astronomical net clean energy. Unlocking commercial fusion promises safe, virtually inexhaustible, emission-free energy to power human prosperity for millennia.',
